From 99f9a26673e6a0f28a0a72b1372f71716811af41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 11:45:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] openwrt: fix the ath10k push-pull tx queue state

Carry three ath10k fixes, submitted to ath-next, as mac80211 package
patches.

ath10k leaves the push-pull queue state of a removed station or vif
set, and it carries the queue state and the push-pull mode over a
firmware restart. Neither depends on the host byte order. After a
restart in push-pull mode a QCA9984 sent no data frame until the new
firmware reported its mode 2.2 s later. The first fix stores the peer
bitmap as little endian. It changes only big-endian hosts and is
carried because the second builds on it.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
